course: dictionary
lesson: 11140
title: Wifi: connecting without wires
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wifi lets your phone, tablet or computer connect to the internet, or to other devices, without wires. It uses radio waves, which carry information through the air. It is also written Wi-Fi. When people say «the wifi is down», they mean the wireless internet in that place has stopped working.
explain: Wifi is a short link. «Wifi is only the short radio link between your device and the router at home.» The router is the box that joins your home network to the internet. The internet is the worldwide network that joins computers together, and wifi is one wireless way to join your device to it.
explain: Wifi and the internet can fail separately. «Checking whether other devices connect helps find which part is broken.» If every device has no connection, the internet may be the problem. If only one device fails, the problem may be that device.
fact: Wifi means connecting devices without wires, using radio waves.
fact: Wifi is also written Wi-Fi.
fact: «The wifi password» is the secret code you type to join a network, so keep it private.
fact: Never join unknown public wifi without an adult.
fact: «The cloud» is not in the sky. It is in data centres, big buildings on the ground full of servers, wires and fans.
exercise: What does «the wifi is down» mean? | The house is very quiet | The router has been moved upstairs | *The wireless internet in this place has stopped working | Everyone has gone home
exercise: What does wifi use to carry information through the air? | Sound from speakers | *Radio waves | Wires | Sunlight
exercise: Ollie's question: what should you do before joining unknown public wifi? | *Ask an adult first | Share the wifi password with your friends | Turn off your router | Join straight away, it is free
test: What is the box that joins your home network to the internet? | A satellite dish | *A router | A data centre | A tablet
test: Where is «the cloud» actually? | In the sky above the town | In the wires under the road | *In data centres, big buildings on the ground full of servers | Inside every phone
exam: Which statement about wifi is true? | Wifi and the cloud are exactly the same thing | *Wifi connects devices without wires, using radio waves | Wifi only works in schools | Wifi needs a wire to join each device
